---
import LegalLayout from "@layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { LEGAL_OPERATOR, LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED, WEBSITE_PROCESSORS } from "@/config/legal";
import { SITE } from "@/config/site";

const breadcrumb = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  itemListElement: [
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: SITE.url },
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Privacy", item: `${SITE.url}/privacy/` },
  ],
};

const op = LEGAL_OPERATOR;
const berlinAuthorityUrl = "https://www.datenschutz-berlin.de/";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  eyebrow="LEGAL"
  description="How the CloudoX website, contact form, and meeting scheduling process personal data, and which service providers are involved."
  lastUpdated={LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED.privacy}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumb]}
>
  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>The controller responsible for processing personal data through this website is:</p>
  <p>
    {op.operatorName}<br />
    trading as {op.tradingName}<br />
    {op.streetAddress}<br />
    {op.postalCode} {op.city}<br />
    {op.country}
  </p>
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${op.legalEmail}`}>{op.legalEmail}</a>
  </p>
  <p>No data-protection officer has been appointed.</p>

  <h2>2. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This notice covers the public CloudoX website, its early-access and
    contact forms, and the meeting-scheduling link. It does not yet govern
    customer cloud-environment discovery or a production SaaS service. Those
    activities will require separate customer contractual and privacy
    documentation before commercial operation.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Website delivery, CDN, and security</h2>
  <p>The website uses Cloudflare for DNS, content delivery, hosting, and security.</p>
  <p>
    When you access the website, Cloudflare and the underlying hosting
    infrastructure may process technical information required to deliver
    and protect the site, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address</li>
    <li>requested URL and file</li>
    <li>date and time of access</li>
    <li>HTTP method and status</li>
    <li>referrer, where provided</li>
    <li>browser and device information</li>
    <li>security and diagnostic information</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Purposes:</strong> delivering the website, maintaining availability and performance, preventing abuse and attacks, and diagnosing technical faults.</p>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Article 6(1)(f) GDPR — legitimate interests
    in providing a secure, reliable, and functional website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare operates a global network, and processing can involve
    infrastructure or systems outside the EEA. Where that occurs, it is
    carried out under Cloudflare's applicable safeguards, including
    contractual transfer mechanisms (see Section 9).
  </p>
  <p>
    Technical data of this kind is retained only for as long as required for
    the operational and security purposes described above, according to
    Cloudflare's account configuration and applicable contractual terms. We
    have not independently verified an exact retention period and do not
    state one we cannot confirm.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Contact and early-access forms</h2>
  <p>
    The website uses <strong>Web3Forms</strong> to process contact and
    early-access submissions and forward them to us by email. The current
    form (at <a href="/contact">/contact</a>) submits exactly the following
    fields:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>name</li>
    <li>email address</li>
    <li>company or role (optional)</li>
    <li>approximate AWS environment scale (optional)</li>
    <li>a free-text message describing your interest</li>
    <li>
      a small amount of technically generated metadata associated with the
      submission (a static subject line, a honeypot anti-spam field that
      stays empty for human visitors, and the public Web3Forms form
      identifier)
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not currently ask for, and you should not submit, AWS credentials,
    account exports, secrets, or other confidential infrastructure data
    through this form.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Purposes:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>responding to your enquiry</li>
    <li>evaluating early-access interest</li>
    <li>communicating about a requested pilot or product discussion</li>
    <li>protecting the form from misuse</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Legal bases:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Article 6(1)(b) GDPR, where processing is necessary to respond to a request connected with potential contractual steps;</li>
    <li>Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, for general business communication, abuse prevention, and managing genuine early-access interest;</li>
    <li>Article 6(1)(a) GDPR (consent) only for processing that is genuinely optional and implemented with a valid opt-in — we do not currently run any such optional processing on this form.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Submitting this form is not treated as, and does not create, marketing
    consent.
  </p>
  <p><strong>How your submission is processed:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>You submit the form.</li>
    <li>Web3Forms processes and forwards the submission.</li>
    <li>The resulting message is received and stored in our IONOS-hosted mailbox.</li>
    <li>{op.operatorName} reviews and responds to it.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Web3Forms states that it does not retain form submissions as stored
    records, but it may temporarily process submission data and maintain
    server logs that can contain personal data; those logs are periodically
    deleted according to Web3Forms' own practice. We do not claim that "your
    information is never stored" — only what is stated above. Web3Forms may
    rely on infrastructure located outside the EEA; see Section 9.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Retention:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>rejected spam or clearly irrelevant submissions: deleted when no longer operationally required;</li>
    <li>ordinary early-access enquiries: retained while the discussion remains active and for a reasonable follow-up period;</li>
    <li>correspondence connected to an actual business relationship: retained according to applicable legal and contractual record-keeping obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not currently commit to a fixed number of months for enquiry
    retention; we are establishing a practical deletion routine for
    abandoned early-access enquiries (see the notice immediately above the
    submit button on the form).
  </p>
  <p>We do not automatically subscribe form submitters to a newsletter.</p>

  <h2>5. Email communication</h2>
  <p>Email communication is hosted by <strong>IONOS</strong>.</p>
  <p>
    When you contact us by email, or through a form forwarded to email, we
    process your contact information, message content, associated metadata,
    and subsequent correspondence to respond to and manage your enquiry.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal bases:</strong> Article 6(1)(b) GDPR for pre-contractual or
    contractual communication; Article 6(1)(f) GDPR for other legitimate
    business communication.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not claim end-to-end encryption for ordinary email. Internet email
    may not be completely secure in transit; please do not send highly
    confidential information through the public contact form or by email.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Meeting scheduling with Zeeg</h2>
  <p>We use Zeeg for optional appointment scheduling, linked from this site — not embedded in it.</p>
  <p>
    When you choose to follow the booking link and schedule a meeting, Zeeg
    may process information such as your name, email address, selected
    appointment, timezone, any answers you enter in the booking form,
    technical information required to provide the booking, and calendar or
    notification information.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Purposes:</strong> displaying availability, arranging the requested appointment, sending confirmations and reminders, and managing changes and cancellations.</p>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Article 6(1)(b) GDPR for requested
    pre-contractual communication, or Article 6(1)(f) GDPR for efficient
    scheduling of business enquiries.
  </p>
  <p>
    Zeeg states that its scheduling data is stored and processed on servers
    in Germany. Because the booking link opens Zeeg's own site, processing
    begins once you follow the link and interact with it there — visiting a
    CloudoX page that merely links to Zeeg does not by itself send Zeeg any
    data.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not set any cookies and does not write to local or
    session storage from its own code. We do not run analytics, advertising
    trackers, or cross-site marketing scripts, and we do not embed
    third-party widgets that load automatically. Fonts are self-hosted
    rather than loaded from a third-party font service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because no technology on this site currently requires consent under the
    ePrivacy rules, we do not show a cookie-consent banner — adding one
    without a technical reason would be misleading rather than helpful. If
    that changes (for example, if we ever add optional analytics), we will
    implement prior consent before any such technology loads and update this
    section accordingly.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Recipients and processors</h2>
  <p>The following providers process website data on our behalf, to the extent described above:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>Role</th>
        <th>Data categories</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {WEBSITE_PROCESSORS.map((p) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{p.name}</td>
          <td>{p.role}</td>
          <td>{p.dataCategories}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    We may also disclose personal data to professional advisers, public
    authorities, or other service providers where legally required or
    necessary.
  </p>

  <h2>9. International data transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some providers we use — particularly globally operating infrastructure
    providers such as Cloudflare, and potentially Web3Forms — may process
    data outside Germany or the EEA. We do not claim that all website data
    remains exclusively in Germany.
  </p>
  <p>Where a transfer outside the EEA occurs, it is made only under an applicable legal mechanism, such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>an adequacy decision,</li>
    <li>the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, or</li>
    <li>another legally recognized safeguard.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>10. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data is retained only as long as needed for the purpose for
    which it was collected and as required by applicable law. Technical
    logs, form submissions, correspondence, and scheduling records may have
    different retention periods, described where relevant above; we state
    processing-specific principles rather than a single invented period that
    covers everything.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you,</li>
    <li>request rectification of inaccurate data,</li>
    <li>request erasure,</li>
    <li>request restriction of processing,</li>
    <li>data portability, where applicable,</li>
    <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests,</li>
    <li>withdraw consent prospectively, where consent is the legal basis, and</li>
    <li>lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The competent supervisory authority for us is the{" "}
    <a href={berlinAuthorityUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Berlin Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information
    </a>{" "}
    (<em>Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit</em>).
  </p>
  <p>
    Requests can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${op.legalEmail}`}>{op.legalEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Obligation to provide data</h2>
  <p>
    You are not generally required to provide personal data merely to browse
    this website. Required form fields are necessary to process the
    enquiry you submit — without them, we may be unable to respond or
    arrange early access.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Automated decision-making</h2>
  <p>
    Website enquiry data is not used for automated decision-making producing
    legal or similarly significant effects.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use appropriate technical and organizational safeguards, including
    encrypted HTTPS transport, restricted administrative access, and the
    security controls of our service providers. No method of transmission
    or storage is completely secure, and we do not promise absolute
    security.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this privacy notice when the website, our providers, or
    applicable legal requirements change. The date above reflects the latest
    update.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
